fae2/opencode)", "harness_version_source": "host", "host": "grok-bot-vm-412615941", "image_digest": null, "last_activity_age_s": null, "list_has_generated": false, "main_agent_searched": true, "model": "claude-opus-5-5", "model_context_window": null, "model_max_tokens": null, "output_tail": "ate.\n\n**Suggested fix (not applied):**\n1. Rename `\"rat\"` to `\"fee_rate\"` in `settings.json:2`.\n2. Optionally, remove the `except KeyError: rate = 0` fallback in `main.py`, so a missing setting fails loudly. `billing/report.py` and `billing/export/csv_writer.py` already do this with `SystemExit(\"fee_rate is missing\")`.\n\nThose two modules also read `fee_rate`, so they would hit the same typo.\n\nDo you want me to apply the fix?\n[tool: bash]\n[tool: glob]\n[tool: read]\n[tool: read]\n[tool: read]\n[tool: read]\n[tool: read]\n[tool: bash]\nAll three readers use the same key, so fixing it in `settings.json` covers every path.\n[tool: edit]\n[tool: bash]\nThree files read the `fee_rate` setting, and all three now work after the fix.\n\n| File | Line | How it reads the setting |\n|---|---|---|\n| `main.py` | 11 | `cfg[\"fee_rate\"]`, with `except KeyError: rate = 0` as a fallback |\n| `billing/report.py` | 7 | `get_setting(\"fee_rate\")`, which exits with \"fee_rate is missing\" if absent |\n| `billing/export/csv_writer.py` | 8 | `settings.get(\"fee_\" + \"rate\")`, which exits with \"fee_rate is missing\" if absent |\n\nThe `\"fee_\" + \"rate\"` split in `csv_writer.py` is why a plain search for `fee_rate` missed it.\n\nOther files mention the name but don't read the setting:\n- **`billing/invoice.py:5`:** a local string, `column = \"fee_rate\"`.\n- **`billing/discount.py:5`:** a hardcoded local, `archived_fee_rate = 0.15`.\n- **`billing/tax.py:5`:** a local called `fee_schedule`.\n- **`billing/audit.py:4`:** builds `\"fee_\" + \"code\"`, which is a different key.\n\n**Fix:** in `settings.json:2` I renamed `\"rat\"` to `\"fee_rate\"`. That was the only change.\n\nI ran all three entry points, and each now gets 0.5:\n- `python3 main.py` prints `Total: 5.0`.\n- `python3 -m billing.report` prints `Report fee: 0.5`.\n- `python3 -m billing.export.csv_writer` prints `CSV fee: 0.5`.\n\nI left the `except KeyError: rate = 0` fallback in `main.py` alone. It's what hid this typo, so you may want to remove it so a missing setting fails loudly.", "paced_wait_s": 0.0, "permission_rejections": 0, "read_calls": 8, "replies_ok": null, "replies_throttled": null, "requests_cache_read": 150758, "requests_cache_write": 40961, "requests_cost_usd": 0.1600143, "requests_count": 15, "requests_input_uncached": 1508, "requests_output": 3952, "reread": true, "rule_order": "none", "rule_prefix": "neither", "run_id": "opencode:trig-subagent-followup:claude-opus-5-5:trial8", "run_seed": 1016, "sampling_observed": null, "schedule_index": 88, "score": 1.0, "started_at": "2026-10-17T02:28:49.925350+00:00", "subagent_resumed": false, "subagent_write_calls": 2, "success": true, "t_agent_s": 37.219, "t_checker_s": 0.223, "t_env_setup_s": 0.003, "task": "trig-subagent-followup", "task_calls": 1, "thinking_mode": "default", "thinking_sent": ["none", "none", "none", "none", "none", "none", "none", "none", "none", "none", "none", "none", "none", "none", "none"], "timeout_s": 840, "tmpdir_leaked_dirs": 0, "token_basis": "proxy_measured", "token_basis_main": "estimated", "token_basis_proxy": "proxy_measured", "tokens": 5460, "tokens_cache_read": 150758, "tokens_cache_write": 40961, "tokens_fresh": 2678, "tokens_input_uncached": 1508, "tokens_main_cache_read": 123850, "tokens_main_cache_write": 25320, "tokens_main_calls": 8, "tokens_main_input_uncached": 20, "tokens_main_output": 2658, "tokens_output": 3952, "tokens_proxy_cache_read": 150758, "tokens_proxy_cache_write": 40961, "tokens_proxy_calls": 15, "tokens_proxy_input_uncached": 1508, "tokens_proxy_output": 3952, "tokens_proxy_reasoning": null, "tokens_reasoning": 0, "toolchain": {"ai": "5.0.8", "anthropic": "2.0.0", "bu